url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123566","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123566.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123566.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nFixes get_executable_path on OpenBSD which had been using OS-local workarounds, but now has getexecpath(3). Closes related PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/61540\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI've kept it simple and close to the __Linux__ section. I'm not sure about the importance of the `append_utf8` method, but applied it here functionally the same as for Linux.\r\n\r\nThe chance of getexecpath(3) failing per the man page are very low; mainly if the directory where the binary was started isn't linked to the file system anymore. With the Godot installation on OpenBSD in /usr/local/bin, this should be extremely unlikely and there would be much bigger issues, so `ERR_FAIL` seemed like the best way to handle this unlikely event.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123566/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}